  <!--
    Neo-Geo native saveram definition.
    saveram size: 65536 bytes (0x10000)

    Neo-Geo saveram is 16-bit byte-swapped.  Applying byte-swap="2" at
    structure level turns each 8-byte score record into the natural layout:

      +0      unused/pad
      +1..+3  SCORE, 3-byte packed BCD
      +4..+6  NAME, 3 ASCII characters
      +7      F.RANK code

    Example real score:
      raw saveram : 20 00 00 84 49 50 00 50
      swap-2      : 00 20 84 00 50 49 50 00
      decoded     : 208400 | PIP | BEGINNER

    Each fighter uses a 0x20-byte slot:
      3 x 8-byte records + 8 unused bytes.
    CONTINUE PLAYER is output last.
  -->

